      "type": "text",
      "text": "If therapy is considered, intralesional triamcinolone is the treatment of choice in adults: 2.5 to 5 mg/mL, 0.1 to 3 mL every 4 to 8 weeks, if the lesions are small. Potent topicals (eg, clobetasol 0.05% 2 times a day for about 4 weeks) often don't reach the hair bulb"
     }
